// Title: Indirect Inline Command Execution Via Bash.EXE
// Sigma ID: 5edc2273-c26f-406c-83f3-f4d948e740dd
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2021-11-24 | Modified: 2023-08-15
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1202
// Description: Detects execution of Microsoft bash launcher with the "-c" flag. This can be used to potentially
//   bypass defenses and execute Linux or Windows-based binaries directly via bash.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Bash/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_bash_command_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith ":\\Windows\\System32\\bash.exe" or FolderPath endswith ":\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\bash.exe") or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "Bash.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains " -c "
